post_message -- {"message": "Hi Gil! Thanks for sharing your info. I have 7 hours availability and my top skills are testing (0.74) and frontend (0.71). Looking at the costs, I see that ISSUE-0001 tasks are much more affordable for me (1.99-4.96) compared to ISSUE-0002 tasks (5.34-10.67), similar to your situation.

Since we both have strong frontend skills and ISSUE-0001 is critical priority, it makes sense for us to focus on those tasks. I'm particularly well-suited for the testing task (ISSUE-0001::test) given my testing skill match, though the cost is a bit higher at 3.47. The triage task would be most efficient for me at 1.99 cost.

Would you like to coordinate which specific ISSUE-0001 tasks we each take? I'm flexible - I could handle testing, triage, or review based on what works best for our overall coverage.", "blackboard_id": 2}

post_message -- {"blackboard_id": 2, "message": "Gil, your proposal makes sense! Taking ISSUE-0001::implement and ISSUE-0001::test would give us good coverage on the critical priority issue. However, I want to make sure we don't leave any gaps on other important subtasks for ISSUE-0001.

Since you have 10h availability, would you consider taking ISSUE-0001::implement (4h) and I take ISSUE-0001::test (2.8h), but then we also consider who handles the remaining tasks? The review (2h) and docs (2h) are both important for the critical issue completion.

Alternatively, if we want to be more conservative with our assignments, your original plan of you taking implement and me taking test works well - we can leave the other subtasks for other agents or future sprints. What are your thoughts on covering more of the ISSUE-0001 subtasks versus focusing on just these two key ones?"}

post_message -- {"blackboard_id": 2, "message": "Gil, given the conflict on ISSUE-0001::implement, I think it makes sense for you to yield to Lorean since their cost is slightly better (3.77 vs 3.79). 

If you take ISSUE-0001::test instead (2.8h, cost 2.65), that would free me up to take ISSUE-0001::review (2h, cost 2.48). This would still give us excellent coverage on the critical priority issue with Lorean on implement, you on test, me on review, and Della on triage.

This allocation would be very efficient cost-wise and ensure we have the key development workflow covered (implement → test → review). What do you think of this revised plan?"}
